  "notes": "Checked, not equivalent to any board entry: the gate reports no exact duplicate and no WL-equivalent entry. No board entry has n = 373. It dominates [[392,8,15]] on (n, k, d, w), which therefore leaves the frontier of every cell the two share. Board entries at the unreduced size n = 392 with k = 8: [[392,8,15]]. The construction and both published reduction moves are from arXiv:2504.08887 (Sec. II, Sec. III D step 4 and Sec. III E; this repository's own research/local2d modules cite Table V of that paper for the family's ungrafted distances and Tables II-IV for its qubit-removal layouts such as [[188,8,9]], which come out of the cleanup rather than the graft), but this parameter set, the capped r=2 merge-graft step and this single-layer layout are not, so novelty is left unknown and literature novelty is unverified.",
